    "note": "Boston’s Museum of Fine Arts with its twin Huntington Avenue limestone wings and stepped central portico, the long Fenway colonnade, an open west courtyard, and the glazed Art of the Americas addition and Shapiro roof. The absolute 3 m datum preserves native terrain and seats the museum on a low exposed granite plinth. Modeled steps connect both street elevations. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
